From u63023c771a070260 at groups.google.com  Tue Oct  2 16:58:06 2012
From: u63023c771a070260 at groups.google.com (Antonio Piccolboni)
Date: Tue, 02 Oct 2012 16:58:06 +0000
Subject: rmr 2.0 released
Message-ID: <X02SSzQTDV0.NEWEs8UDDuEJ@rhadoop.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rhadoop/c/X02SSzQTDV0/m/NEWEs8UDDuEJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

All vectorized, first class support for structured data, deeply refactored.
My favorite and new example: counting distinct items <https://github.com/RevolutionAnalytics/RHadoop/blob/master/rmr2/pkg/examples/counts.R>
Changelog <https://github.com/RevolutionAnalytics/RHadoop/wiki/Changelog>
New in this release <https://github.com/RevolutionAnalytics/RHadoop/blob/6333a200f2501e6e9190ad872c413c8f13a178ab/rmr2/docs/new-in-this-release.md>
If you liked the Tutorial <https://github.com/RevolutionAnalytics/RHadoop/blob/master/rmr2/docs/tutorial.md>, take a second look, all the examples are shorter and simpler.
Take it  <https://github.com/downloads/RevolutionAnalytics/RHadoop/rmr2_2.0.0.tar.gz>for a spin and let me know what you think

Antonio

